From 669c9586aa6d2c8cb3a149e95160acade9dbc0c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 356/488] soh: name the 19 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_du.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 19 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Du/z_en_du.c.

  * func_809FDDB4 -> EnDu_ShouldSpawn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: Init kills the actor when this returns 0; true
    only in Goron City as child, or in the Fire Temple as adult before
    INFTABLE_SPOKE_TO_DARUNIA_IN_FIRE_TEMPLE

  * func_809FDE24 -> EnDu_TrackPlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: feeds the player's position to Npc_TrackPoint,
    disabling head tracking while idle or mid-cutscene

  * func_809FDE9C -> EnDu_UpdateFace
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the blink timer and picks the eye, mouth
    and nose texture indices from unk_1EC/unk_1ED/unk_1EE

  * func_809FDFC0 -> EnDu_GetCueStartPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies a CsCmdActorCue's startPos into the
    caller's Vec3f

  * func_809FE000 -> EnDu_GetCueEndPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies a CsCmdActorCue's endPos into the
    caller's Vec3f

  * func_809FE040 -> EnDu_AdvanceDanceAnim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steps an eight-entry animation ring at each
    animation end -- the body of Darunia's dance, cue 7

  * func_809FE104 -> EnDu_AdvanceDanceFinishAnim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steps a four-entry animation sequence once and
    stops -- the wind-down of the dance, cue 8

  * func_809FE3B4 -> EnDu_DoNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: empty action, installed for adult Link outside
    the Fire Temple

  * func_809FE3C0 -> EnDu_WaitForOcarina
    deduced, confidence HIGH: idles as an ocarina-listening NPC, flagging
    PLAYER_STATE2_NEAR_OCARINA_ACTOR in range and starting the song prompt
    when the player plays

  * func_809FE4A4 -> EnDu_CheckOcarinaSong
    deduced, confidence HIGH: reads msgCtx.ocarinaMode and triggers either
    gGoronCityDaruniaCorrectCs or gGoronCityDaruniaWrongCs

  * func_809FE638 -> EnDu_FireTempleStartScene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: once the player leaves its cutscene, opens a
    OnePointCutscene, faces the player at Darunia and plays NA_BGM_APPEAR

  * func_809FE6CC -> EnDu_FireTempleWaitToTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts unk_1E2 down from 0x32, then opens
    textbox 0x3039

  * func_809FE740 -> EnDu_FireTempleWaitTalkDone
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for the talk state to return to idle,
    releases the camera and arms the 0x5A departure timer

  * func_809FE798 -> EnDu_FireTempleDepart
    deduced, confidence HIGH: slides Darunia out through the door with the
    unlock/open/close/thud sounds, then kills the actor and sets
    INFTABLE_SPOKE_TO_DARUNIA_IN_FIRE_TEMPLE

  * func_809FE890 -> EnDu_PerformCutsceneAction
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drives position, rotation and animation from
    csCtx.npcActions[2], including the dance cues 7 and 8

  * func_809FEB08 -> EnDu_EndDanceCutscene
    deduced, confidence HIGH: resets the face, and either returns to the
    ocarina wait (wrong song) or starts the reward text

  * func_809FEC14 -> EnDu_WaitToGiveReward
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for the talk state to reach
    NPC_TALK_STATE_ACTION, then enters the give-item action immediately

  * func_809FEC70 -> EnDu_GiveGoronBracelet
    deduced, confidence HIGH: offers GI_BRACELET until the player takes it

  * func_809FECE4 -> EnDu_WaitForItemGiven
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out NPC_TALK_STATE_ITEM_GIVEN and
    returns to the ocarina wait

